{
  "slug": "js_meta_proxy",
  "course": "js",
  "order": 240,
  "url": "/js/js_meta_proxy.asp",
  "title": "JavaScript Proxy",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "JavaScript Proxy"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "What is a Proxy?"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "A Proxy is a JavaScript object that can wrap other objects."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "A Proxy lets you control operations on other objects."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "A Proxy can trap and intercept code when someone is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "Reading a property (get)",
        "Setting a property (set)",
        "Deleting a property (deleteProperty)",
        "Checking if a property exists (has)",
        "Calling a function (apply)",
        "Constructing an object (construct)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "A Proxy lets you run your own code when someone interacts with an object."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "A Proxy gan be a middleman between your code and a JavaScript object."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const proxy = new Proxy(target, handler);",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["target - the original object or function", "handler - an object with trap methods"]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const myObject = {name: \"Jan\"};\n\nconst proxy = new Proxy(myObject, {\n\n  get(target, prop) {\n\n    return target[prop];\n\n  }\n\n});",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Proxy Logging"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "A typical Proxy example is logging of object changes."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Below is a demo that:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "Wraps an object in a Proxy",
        "Logs whenever a property is read or written",
        "Logs each get and set operation in real time"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "// Create an Object\n\nconst user = { name: \"Jan\", age: 40 };\n\n//Create a Proxy\n\nconst proxy = new Proxy(user, {\n\n  get(target, property) {\n\n    log(\"Getting: \" + property);\n\n    return target[property];\n\n  },\n\n  set(target, property, value) {\n\n    log(\"Setting: \" + property);\n\n    return target[property];\n\n  }\n\n});\n\nproxy.name = \"John\";\n\nproxy.age = 42;\n\nlet text1 = proxy.name;\n\nlet text2 = proxy.age",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_proxy"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Proxy with Reflect (Most Common)"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Below is a demo that:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "Wraps an object in a Proxy",
        "Logs whenever a property is read or written",
        "Uses Reflect.get() and Reflect.set() inside the Proxy handlers",
        "get trap uses Reflect.get(target, property, receiver)",
        "set trap uses Reflect.set(target, property, value, receiver)",
        "Reflect makes the Proxy behavior match the normal object behavior"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "// Create an Object\n\nconst user = { name: \"Jan\", age: 40 };\n\n// Create a Proxy\n\nconst proxy = new Proxy(user, {\n\n  get(target, property) {\n\n    log(\"Getting: \" + property);\n    // safe forwarding\n\n    return Reflect.get(target, property);\n\n  },\n\n  set(target, property, value) {\n\n    log(\"Setting: \" + property);\n    // safe forwarding\n\n    return Reflect.set(target, property, value);\n\n  }\n\n});\n\nproxy.name = \"John\";\n\nproxy.age = 42;\n\nlet text1 = proxy.name;\n\nlet text2 = proxy.age",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_proxy_reflect"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Proxy with Reflect Flow"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The flow below is the essence of JavaScript metaprogramming with Proxy + Reflect."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Flow Explanation:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "Your code interacts with an object",
        "Proxy intercepts the operation",
        "Your trap code decides what to do",
        "Reflect forwards the operation safely",
        "The target object receives the real action"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Why Proxies?"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Proxies allow you to:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "Add logging",
        "Validate changes",
        "Auto-generate properties",
        "Protect sensitive data",
        "Create virtual or computed objects",
        "Intercept function calls",
        "Create reactive systems (like Vue.js)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Proxy Validation"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "// Create an Object\n\nconst user = { name: \"Jan\", age: 40 };\n\n// Create a Proxy\n\nconst proxy = new Proxy(user, {\n\n  set(target, prop, value) {\n\n    if (prop === \"age\" && value < 0) {\n\n      text = \"Age cannot be negative!\";\n\n      document.getElementById(\"demo\").innerHTML = text;\n\n    }\n\n    return Reflect.set(target, prop, value);\n\n  }\n\n});\n\nproxy.age = 45;  // OK\n\nproxy.age = -5;  // Error",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_proxy_validate"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Virtual Properties"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "// Create an Object\n\nconst person = {\n\n  first: \"John\",\n\n  last:  \"Doe\"\n\n};\n\n// Create a Proxy\n\nconst virtual = new Proxy(person, {\n\n  get(target, prop) {\n\n    if (prop === \"fullName\") {\n\n      return target.first + \" \" + target.last;\n\n    }\n\n    return Reflect.get(target, prop);\n\n  }\n\n});\n\nlet text = virtual.fullName; // \"John Doe\"",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_proxy_virtual"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Dynamic Functions"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const fn = new Function(\"a\", \"b\", \"return a + b\");\n\nlet result = fn(3, 2);",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_proxy_dynamic"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Metaprogramming"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Metaprogramming lets JavaScript:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "Intercept behavior",
        "Modify behavior",
        "Define new behavior",
        "Generate behavior dynamically"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "It gives developers deep control over the language's inner workings."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Proxy Traps"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "A trap is a function inside a Proxy handler."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "It runs whenever a specific operation is performed on the Proxy."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Below is a complete and accurate explanation of every JavaScript Proxy trap, what triggers them,\ntheir parameters, and what they are expected to return."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": ["Trap Name", "Triggered when"],
      "rows": [
        ["get", "A property is read"],
        ["set", "A property is changed"],
        ["has", "Using the in operator"],
        ["deleteProperty", "A property is deleted"],
        ["apply", "A function is called"],
        ["construct", "An object is cretated (with new)"],
        ["getOwnPropertyDescriptor", "A property descriptor is retrieved"],
        ["defineProperty", "A property is defined"],
        ["getPrototypeOf", "A prototype is retrieved"],
        ["setPrototypeOf", "A prototype is set"],
        ["isExtensible", "Extensibility is checked"],
        ["preventExtensions", "Existenibility is prevented"],
        ["ownKeys", "Properties are listed"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The list above is 2025-accurate and includes all 13 Proxy traps defined in ECMAScript."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Each trap handler is decribed below."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "handler.get()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Triggered when a property is read:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "get(obj, prop, receiver) {\n\n  return Reflect.get(obj, prop, receiver);\n\n}",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "proxy.property\n\nproxy[\"property\"]\n\nobject.property()",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Parameters"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "obj - the target object",
        "prop - the property being accessed",
        "receiver - the this value for getters (usually the proxy itself)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Must Return"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["The property value"]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "handler.set()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Triggered when a property is assigned a value:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "set(obj, prop, value, receiver) {\n\n  return Reflect.set(obj, prop, value, receiver);\n\n}",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "proxy.property = value;\n\nproxy[\"property\"] = value;",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Parameters"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "obj - the target object",
        "prop - the property being set",
        "value - the new property value",
        "receiver - the object that received the assignment (usually the proxy)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Must Return"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["true - if the assignment succeeded", "false - if the assignment failed"]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Throwing an error is also allowed."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "handler.has()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Intercepts the in operator."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "has(obj, prop) {\n\n  return Reflect.has(obj, prop);\n\n}",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "\"property\" in proxy",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Parameters"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "obj - the target object",
        "prop - the property being accessed",
        "receiver - the value of this for setters (usually the proxy itself)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Must Return"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["true", "false"]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "handler.deleteProperty()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Intercepts the delete operator."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "deleteProperty(obj, prop) {\n\n  return Reflect.deleteProperty(obj, prop);\n\n}",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "delete proxy.property",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Parameters"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["obj - the target object", "prop - the property to delete"]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Must Return"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["true - for sucess", "false - for failure"]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "handler.apply()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Triggered when a function is called:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "apply(func, thisArg, args) {\n\n  return Reflect.apply(func, this, args);\n\n}",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "proxy()\n\nproxy.call()\n\nproxy.apply()",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Parameters"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "func - the callable object (function)",
        "this - the this argument for the call",
        "args - the function arguments array"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Must Return"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["The return value of the function"]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "handler.construct"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Intercepts the new operator."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "construct(obj, args, newTarget) {\n\n  return Reflect.construct(obj, args, newTarget);\n\n}",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "nex proxy()",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Parameters"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "obj - the constructor object",
        "args - the array of arguments passed",
        "newTarget - the constructor"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Must Return"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["An Object (The new instance)"]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const obj = {}  // No trap\n\nObject.create() // No trap\n\nclass User {};\n\nnew User();     // No trap",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "handler.getOwnPropertyDescriptor()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Intercepts property descriptor retrieval."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "getOwnPropertyDescriptor(obj, prop) {\n\n  return Reflect.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(obj, prop);\n\n}",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(obj, prop)",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Parameters"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["obj - the target object", "prop - the property to describe"]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Must Return"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["A property descriptor", "undefined"]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "handler.defineProperty()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Intercepts Object.defineProperty()."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "defineProperty(obj, prop, descriptor) {\n\n  return Reflect.defineProperty(obj, prop, descriptor);\n\n}",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Object.defineProperty()",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Parameters"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "obj - the target object",
        "prop - the property to describe",
        "descriptor - the property descriptor"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Must Return"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["true - if sucess", "false - if not"]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "handler.getPrototypeOf()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Intercepts prototype lookup."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "getPrototypeOf(obj) {\n\n  return Reflect.getPrototypeOf(obj);\n\n}",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Object.getPrototypeOf()",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Parameters"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["obj - the target object"]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Must Return"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["An Object", "null"]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "handler.setPrototypeOf()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Intercepts setting the prototype."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "setPrototypeOf(obj, prototype) {\n\n  return Reflect.setPrototypeOf(obj, prototype);\n\n}",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Object.settPrototypeOf()",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Parameters"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["obj - the target object", "prototype - the new prototype or null"]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Must Return"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["An Object", "null"]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "handler.isExtensible()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Intercepts checking if an object is extensible."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "isExtensible(obj) {\n\n  return Reflect.isExtensible(obj);\n\n}",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Object.isExtensible()",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Parameters"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["obj - the target object"]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Must Return"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["true - for yes", "false - for no"]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "handler.preventExtentions()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Intercepts making an object non-extensible."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "preventExtensions(obj) {\n\n  return Reflect.preventExtensions(obj);\n\n}",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Object.preventExtensions()",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Parameters"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["obj - the target object"]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Must Return"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["true - for success", "false - for failure"]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "handler.ownKeys()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Intercepts operations listing keys (property names or symbols)."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "ownKeys(obj) {\n\n  return Reflect.ownKeys(obj);\n\n}",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "Object.keys()\n\nObject.getOwnPropertyNames()\n\nObject.getOwnPropertySymbols()",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Parameters"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["obj - the target object"]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Must Return"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["array of keys with no duplicates"]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Proxy Traps Map Reflect Methods"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "A Proxy trap represents one of JavaScript's internal operations:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "[[Construct]]",
        "[[Call]]",
        "[[Get]]",
        "[[Set]]",
        "[[HasProperty]]",
        "[[Delete]]",
        "[[DefineProperty]]",
        "[[GetOwnProperty]]",
        "[[OwnPropertyKeys]]",
        "[[GetPrototypeOf]]",
        "[[SetPrototypeOf]]",
        "[[PreventExtensions]]",
        "[[IsExtensible]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "These internal operations are what JavaScript uses (inside the engine) when you access or modify objects."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "When a Proxy intercepts one of these operations, they should be forwarded correctly:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "get(target, property, receiver) {\n\n  return Reflect.get(target, property, receiver);\n\n}",
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Reflect is used because Reflect methods are 1-to-1 mirrors of the internal operations."
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "They produce correct return values (true/false/descriptor)",
        "They avoid throwing errors that would break Proxy rules",
        "They make the Proxy behave like normal JavaScript objects (unless modified)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "This is why every Proxy trap has a Reflect method with the same name and signature."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "JavaScript Internals Became Reflect"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Before ES6 (2015), many fundamental operations did not exist as functions:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [],
      "rows": [
        ["Operation", "Before E6", "Problem"],
        ["get property", "obj[prop]", "Not callable as a function"],
        ["set property", "obj[prop] = value", "Not callable as a function"],
        ["delete property", "delete obj[prop]", "Operator, not a function"],
        ["check property", "\"prop\" in obj", "Operator, not a function"],
        ["construct (new)", "new Foo()", "Not callable generically"],
        ["get prototypes", "Object.getPrototypeOf(obj)", "Throws on non-objects"],
        ["define property", "Object.defineProperty()", "Returns object instead of boolean"],
        ["own keys", "Object.keys()", "Not complete (misses symbols)"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "These were incomplete and inconsistent for Proxy forwarding."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "So ES6 (2015) added Reflect:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": ["Internal Operation", "Reflect Method"],
      "rows": [
        ["[[Construct]]", "Reflect.construct()"],
        ["[[Call]]", "Reflect.apply()"],
        ["[[Get]]", "Reflect.get()"],
        ["[[Set]]", "Reflect.set()"],
        ["[[HasProperty]]", "Reflect.has()"],
        ["[[Delete]]", "Reflect.deleteProperty()"],
        ["[[DefineProperty]]", "Reflect.defineProperty()"],
        ["[[GetOwnProperty]]", "Reflect.getOwnProperty()"],
        ["[[OwnPropertyKeys]]", "Reflect.ownPropertyKeys()"],
        ["[[IsExstensible]]", "Reflect.isExtensible()"],
        ["[[PreventExstensions]]", "Reflect.preventExtensions()"],
        ["[[GetPrototypeOf]]", "Reflect.getPrototypeOf()"],
        ["[[SetPrototypeOf]]", "Reflect.setPrototypeOf()"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Learn More"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "JavaScript Metaprogramming"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "JavaScript Reflect Tutorial"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "JavaScript Meta Reference"
    }
  ]
